Task: step-events-tests + step-events-impl (plan agui_workflow_graph_b7e4d091, phase P2)

Why: FR1. Attribution rides AG-UI's existing STEP_* events because the
pinned Go SDK has no event-level metadata (that gap belongs to
aguiproto_20260908), so the step name is the only channel available for
per-event provenance in this track.

Changes:
- agui/internal/stream/processor.go: step key computed from node
  provenance when present, author otherwise; State.CurrentStepAuthor
  renamed CurrentStepName.
- agui/graph_steps_test.go (new): 6 cases.
- Mechanical rename across agui/stream_test.go.

Design decisions:
- Node steps skip the RootAppName normalisation that plain events get.
  A workflow node whose agent happens to be named like the root is still
  a distinct graph activation; normalising it away would silently drop a
  node. The 'root-named workflow node still gets a step' test pins this,
  and it was one of the two subtests that failed red.
- Kept two separate conditions rather than one: stepMayChange preserves
  the existing 'ev.Author != ""' guard for non-workflow events (so an
  authorless event cannot close an open step) while letting a workflow
  event with a path but no author open one.
- STEP_STARTED now emits the computed step name rather than ev.Author.
  These are equal for every non-workflow case that reaches the emit (the
  root is excluded by the non-empty check), which is why the plain-agent
  golden is unchanged.

